# Canonical public-exposure match list — TEMPLATE
# v1. Copy this to `match-list.grep` alongside it, replace every placeholder with
# your own real terms, and keep YOUR filled copy out of any public repo — the
# filled file is an inventory of exactly the names you are trying to protect.
# Add `references/match-list.grep` to .gitignore, or keep it in private notes and
# point the skill's $ML variable at that path.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: in the originating setup, a pre-merge safety grep ran a
# narrower term list than the post-push live verify — a few terms were present in
# one and absent from the other, because both were re-typed inline at the point of
# use. The narrower screen was the one gating the irreversible step. Nothing leaked
# that time. The fix is structural: one versioned file, read by every pass —
# step-1 working tree, step-4 history, the remediation live verify, and any
# pre-merge check a session improvises. Bump the version + date on any term change.
#
# FORMAT: one extended-regex (ERE) pattern per line, matched case-insensitively.
# Comment lines start with '#' — strip them before use:
#   grep -v '^#' match-list.grep | grep -rniE --exclude-dir=.git -f - .
#
# INTERPRETATION (same as step 1 of the skill): any hit in a public-bound repo is
# a finding; the question is genericize / delete / deliberate-approved
# self-reference. Your own brands may be legitimately public in their OWN branded
# repos by explicit disposition — never by default, and never silently. Legal- or
# regulatory-matter vocabulary has no approved bucket at all. Eyeball every hit;
# generic-word collisions are dismissed per-hit and never by trimming the list,
# because a trimmed list re-creates the failure this file exists to prevent.

# --- employers / practices / brands ---
your-employer-name
your-practice-brand
former-employer

# --- vendors / products tied to the real job ---
your-ehr-vendor
your-lab-vendor
your-messaging-vendor
vendor-tool-prefix-

# --- people (colleagues / contacts — roles are fine, names never) ---
supervisor-surname
colleague-surname
attorney-surname

# --- internal content / character / codenames ---
internal-project-codename
teaching-character-name

# --- matter vocabulary — zero tolerance, no approved bucket ---
regulator-name
your-case-number
matter-specific-phrase
